  "notes": "COMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ⟦{身|み}→身：01764_mi⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧よじる: to writhe, squirm (from pain, tickling, or trying to get free)\n- ⟦{腹|はら}→腹：02165_hara⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧よじって⟦{笑|わら}う→笑う：00685_warau⟧: to double over with laughter (⟦{腹|はら}→腹：02165_hara⟧⟦が→が：00051_ga⟧よじれる, to split one's sides)\n- ⟦{腕|うで}→腕：01006_ude⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧よじる: to twist someone's arm\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{捩|ね}じる→捩じる：04474_nejiru⟧: to twist; the everyday word for objects (a lid, wire, a cap); よじる is mostly used of bodies\n- ⟦{捻|ひね}る→捻る：00102_hineru⟧: to twist, turn (a tap, one's head); more general\n- ⟦{絞|しぼ}る→絞る：03926_shiboru⟧: to wring, squeeze (a towel)\n\nWATCH OUT:\nよじ{登|のぼ}る (to clamber up) comes from a different verb, {攀|よ}じる (to cling), not from this one.",
